  "notes": "The other Dangerous Crew record, and the model is deliberately Too Short's method with Ant Banks' \"harder-hitting\" harmony rather than a second copy of it: the same sampled-funk-kit-plus-live-drums hybrid and swung 16ths with a tambourine layer, but a denser kick, a harder ghost pattern, and a chord set that moves — `i–iv–VII` and `i–VII–VI` with a blues-coloured lead — where Too Short sits on two-chord funk vamps. Live keys, organ and guitar rather than sampled synths, with a clav or wah counter-line, so `countermelody.densityRatio` is the highest in this batch at 0.55 and the counter sits above the lead. Played live bass with a syncopated funk line plus sub reinforcement gives it a low `followRootsProb` and a high glide, but less free than Too Short's, whose bass the research singles out as the defining layer. ⚠ `medium` is the research's rating. INFERRED: the progressions — \"funk-modal … minor vamps with blues color\" is the whole harmonic claim, so the two moving families are inference inside that description and carry the chord part's variety. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 48 to 46 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 47 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 2.",
